implementationPlan.description:
UNDERSTAND THE SEAM before writing either enumerator (read-only step). Getting this wrong makes the tests assert against a helper instead of production, which epic rail 6 forbids.

An enumerator is `RecoveryInventoryEnumerator = (context: RecoveryInventoryEnumerationContext) => unknown` (recovery-inventory-contract.ts:157). It returns exactly one of three shapes, validated by readPortResult (recovery-inventory-shape.ts:202), typed as RecoveryInventoryPortReading (contract:171):
  { status: "ENUMERATED", items: readonly unknown[], complete: boolean, negativeProofDigest: string | null }
  { status: "UNAVAILABLE" }
  { status: "UNSUPPORTED" }

THE ENUMERATOR DOES NOT MINT COVERAGE CODES. collectRecoveryInventory (recovery-inventory.ts:68) maps a reading to a RecoveryInventoryCoverageProof carrying code RECOVERY_INVENTORY_COVERAGE_UNKNOWN, layer INVENTORY_ADAPTER and one RecoveryInventoryUnknownReason. Your job is to return the honest reading; the aggregate produces the refusal. That is why every DoD 3 case must be asserted END-TO-END through collectRecoveryInventory, never by unit-testing a private mapping helper inside your module.

VOCABULARIES ALREADY EXIST — INVENT NOTHING. Classes (contract:24): this slice owns PROVIDER_PROCESS_LAUNCH_LOCK and WORKSPACE only; GIT_INTEGRATION_ON_DISK and ARTIFACT_OBJECT_STAGING are slice 3's. Layers: exactly ["INVENTORY_ADAPTER"]. Truth: ["COMPLETE","UNKNOWN"]. Unknown reasons (contract:57) already cover every DoD 3 case: ENUMERATOR_UNREGISTERED, ENUMERATOR_UNAVAILABLE, ENUMERATOR_FAILED, CAPABILITY_UNSUPPORTED, RESULT_MALFORMED, RESULT_TRUNCATED, RESULT_OVER_LIMIT, NEGATIVE_PROOF_MISSING, ITEM_REJECTED. Duplicate identity has its own code: RECOVERY_INVENTORY_EXTERNAL_IDENTITY_DUPLICATE.

CONSUME THESE SHAPE HELPERS, DO NOT REBUILD THEM: identityKey (shape:121) for duplicate detection, readInventoryItem (:164), readOpaqueRef (:71), readWindow (:85), readIdentity (:106). Item shape (contract:105): { class, projectTag, identity, observedAt, facts, sourceProofDigest }. Ceilings: MAX_RECOVERY_INVENTORY_ITEMS 4096, MAX_RECOVERY_INVENTORY_TEXT_CHARS 400, MAX_RECOVERY_INVENTORY_FACTS 32.
